From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: WorkBuddy AI <noreply@workbuddy.local>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 00:10:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] net: airoha: make threaded NAPI opt-in

The driver forces threaded NAPI on for every QDMA RX queue. On AN7581 the
QDMA exposes a large number of queues, so this spawns a kthread per queue
and costs a scheduler wakeup on every NAPI poll.

Measured on Gemtek XG2010G (AN7581PT, 4x A53 @1200MHz): the qdma_eth NAPI
kthreads consume 102.9% of one core while forwarding ~2 Gbps, i.e. roughly
7357 cycles/packet, about an order of magnitude above the usual budget.
That single term dominates the CPU forwarding path and is the reason the
device cannot approach 10G without hardware offload.

Expose the knob instead of hardcoding it, so a single image can A/B test
both modes:

  - default (off): NAPI runs in softirq context, the classic path
  - airoha_eth.threaded_napi=1 on the kernel cmdline, or
    echo 1 > /sys/module/airoha_eth/parameters/threaded_napi (needs reboot)

Signed-off-by: WorkBuddy AI <noreply@workbuddy.local>
---
 drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c | 14 ++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c
@@ -23,8 +23,18 @@
 #include "airoha_regs.h"
 #include "airoha_eth.h"
 
 static const struct net_device_ops airoha_netdev_ops;
 
+/*
+ * Threaded NAPI spawns a kthread per RX queue. On AN7581 the QDMA exposes
+ * many queues, so this costs a scheduler wakeup on every NAPI poll:
+ * ~7357 cycles/packet measured on XG2010G, ~10x the usual budget, which
+ * caps the CPU forwarding path at ~2 Gbps. Keep it opt-in for A/B tests.
+ */
+static bool threaded_napi;
+module_param(threaded_napi, bool, 0644);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(threaded_napi, "Use kthreads for RX NAPI (default: off)");
+
 u32 airoha_rr(void __iomem *base, u32 offset)
 {
 	return readl(base + offset);
@@ -4760,8 +4770,8 @@
 	if (!eth->napi_dev)
 		return -ENOMEM;
 
-	/* Enable threaded NAPI by default */
-	eth->napi_dev->threaded = true;
+	/* Threaded NAPI is opt-in, see threaded_napi above */
+	eth->napi_dev->threaded = threaded_napi;
 	strscpy(eth->napi_dev->name, "qdma_eth", sizeof(eth->napi_dev->name));
 	platform_set_drvdata(pdev, eth);
 
